==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈmɪz.əl/|/ˈmɪz.l̩/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪzəl}}

===Etymology 1===
Late {{inh|en|enm|misellen||to drizzle}}, cognate with {{cog|nds|miseln}}, {{m|nds|musseln||to mizzle}}, {{cog|nl|miezelen||to drizzle, rain gently}}. Of obscure origin, possibly a frequentative related to the base of {{m|en|mist}}; or, related to {{der|en|gml|mes||urine}}, {{der|en|dum|mes}}, {{m|dum|mis||urine}}, both from {{cog|osx|mehs||urine}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*mihstuz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihstaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mihsk-||urine}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*mīganą||to urinate}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*meiǵʰ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*omeiǵʰ-||to urinate}}. Compare also {{cog|en|micturate||to urinate}}, {{cog|ofs|mese||urine}}, {{cog|nds|miegen||to urinate}}, {{cog|nl|mijgen||to urinate}}, {{cog|da|mige||to urinate}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|mizzl}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|now|_|regional|UK|North America}} To [[rain]] in very fine drops.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|rain in very fine drops}} {{l|en|drizzle}}

